{"title":"Composter","slug":"Composter","hero":{"file":"Composter.webp","width":400,"height":396},"pageid":3240,"revid":22040,"timestamp":"2026-07-06T14:29:58Z","lastEditor":"Sdgthpkghfjpk","categories":[],"infobox":{"type":"Objects","fields":[{"label":"Island","value":"Flowering Meadows"},{"label":"Shop","value":"Flora Laura"},{"label":"Price","value":"10,760$"},{"label":"Version Added","value":"1.66.2"},{"label":"Function","value":"Сreates dirt by putting a lot of flowers, plants into the Composter."},{"label":"Date Added","value":"30.08.2024"}]},"sections":[{"id":"description","text":"Description"},{"id":"method-of-application","text":"Method of application"},{"id":"composting","text":"Composting"},{"id":"notes","text":"Notes"}],"body":"<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p><i><big>\"Fill up with plant matter to produce dirt! Dirt will always come out where the arrow faces.\"</big></i>\n</p>\n<h2 id=\"method-of-application\">Method of application</h2>\n<ul><li>With dirt, you can refine and can forge it. Also, you can fill schematics with it.</li></ul>\n<p>Players can throw any flowers and fruits into the composter and the like.\n</p><p><b>Attention</b>: Filling a composter can be difficult, you really need a lot of resources to fill at least 1 composter.\n</p>\n<h6 id=\"tip-a-single-tumbleweed-cattail-or-water-lily-can-fill-the-entire-composter-instantly\">Tip: A single Tumbleweed, Cattail or Water Lily can fill the entire composter instantly.</h6><p>\nOnce the composter is completely full, you will not be able to load any biomaterials into it, then you had to wait about 1 minute or a little more, and then a lump of earth will form next to it, and the composter itself will be empty.</p><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"> \t<span role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: Filling the composter.\">Filling the composter.</span> \t \t<figcaption> \t\t \t\t\t<span data-unresolved=\"1\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></span> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p>Filling the composter.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"> \t<span role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: Results of the work.\">Results of the work.</span> \t \t<figcaption> \t\t \t\t\t<span data-unresolved=\"1\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></span> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p>Results of the work.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n\n<h2 id=\"composting\">Composting</h2>\n<p>Each plant in the game has different composting levels and percentages; you can check the percentage of how much your composter got filled by a plant by using a <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/Statistic_Tool/\">Statistic Tool</a>.\n</p><p>Here's the current composting percentage for some plants in the game: (WIP)\n</p>\n<div class=\"ok-tablewrap\"><table>\n<caption>\nPlant Composter Percentage\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Image\n</th>\n<th>Plant\n</th>\n<th>Compost&#160;%\n</th>\n<th>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><span role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: Tumbleweed\">Tumbleweed</span></span>\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/Tumbleweed/\">Tumbleweed</a>\n</td>\n<td>100%\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"> \t<span role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: Cattail\">Cattail</span> \t<noscript><span class=\"ok-media-placeholder\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: Cattail\">Cattail</span></noscript> \t<figcaption> \t\t \t\t\t<span data-unresolved=\"1\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></span> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/Cattail/\">Cattail</a>\n</td>\n<td>100%\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"> \t<span role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: Water Lily\">Water Lily</span> \t<noscript><span class=\"ok-media-placeholder\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: Water Lily\">Water Lily</span